And while it might be a work of non-fiction, it��s set to grip you as much as any of his fictional thrillers.
Here��s what you need to know about the new series.
When is The Innocent Man released on Netflix?
The series will be released in its entirety on Friday December 14.
There are six instalments in total, which will likely be released at around 8am, the time that most new shows are released on to Netflix on a Friday.
Who does the series focus on?
The series focuses on four men accused of two separate murders (Picture: Netflix)
The focus is on four men who were jailed for two separate murders in the town of Ada, Oklahoma, in 1982 and 1984.
Ron Williamson and Dennis Fritz were convicted of killing waitress Debbie Carte, who was found raped and murdered in 1982, and had writing on her body in ketchup.
Williamson was sentenced to death and Fritz – who was not charged until five years later – to life in prison.
However, new evidence 11 years later revealed that DNA on the victim did not match theirs, but another man, Glenn Gore.
