And you know what? Wow. That's what.
We were amazed by the Olympic Park. We were impressed by the organization. And mostly we were overwhelmed by the British themselves. We normally see them grimly shuffling to work, swearing at their athletes and enduring the challenges of living in London. But the Olympics has put them in a different light. Despite what you may have been hearing in the media, we've watched an entire country of volunteers and organizers enthusiastically come together to pull off an amazing feat: hosting the world, cheering for Team GB, having a good time and putting on a fantastic show.
The British have taught me a few things this week. And I plan to take these lessons back to my business in America.
